.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt RETICULUM-GO-COMPLETION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reticulum-go-completion
.Nd print shell completion scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm reticulum-go Cm completion
.Cm bash | zsh | fish
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Prints a shell completion script on standard output.
The script is generated from the same flag sets used by the tools.
It completes subcommands, flag names, and file paths for flags that take paths.
.Pp
Bash example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
reticulum-go completion bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/reticulum-go
.Ed
.Pp
Zsh example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
reticulum-go completion zsh > ~/.zsh/site-functions/_reticulum-go
.Ed
.Pp
Fish example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
reticulum-go completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/reticulum-go.fish
.Ed
.Pp
Linux packages install the bash, zsh, and fish scripts under the system completion directories.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reticulum-go 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Quad4.io
